    {
      "id": "AWH-01",
      "chapter": "lifts",
      "title": "A signature and a polynomial Gaussian determine the archimedean section",
      "anchor": "lifts-archimedean-whittaker",
      "statement": "For one real place, the source test is P(X,X̅) exp(−c Σ|Xᵢⱼ|²) and the positive Gram transform is A(Y)=∫P exp(−c‖X‖²)exp(it tr(YX*JX))dX. The Whittaker Fourier transform at B uses the phase exp(−it tr(BY)), the weight det(I+Y²)^{−w}, and w=z−(M−n)/2.",
      "hypotheses": "Choose Hermitian frames of signature (p,q), p+q=M, a nontrivial place character with t=2πℓ, c=|t|=2π|ℓ|>0, and arbitrary polynomial P in the matrix entries and their conjugates. The regular target is Hermitian and det B≠0. The coordinate theorem uses Lebesgue measure in n² real Hermitian coordinates.",
