      "title": "Repeated determinant differentiation gives an entire function at a nonsingular frequency",
      "anchor": "lifts-archimedean-continuation",
      "statement": "The Nth regularized Fourier integral divides the transform of Δ^N(D^{−w}A) by ((it)^n det B)^N. It is holomorphic for 2 Re w+M+N>n². These half-planes cover ℂ and the integrals agree by analytic uniqueness. The provider identifies the ordinary absolutely convergent integral with the result on Re w>n²/2.",
