      "status": "mathematical proof reconstructed",
      "correspondence": "The signed row Gaussians yield resolvents (I∓i sign(ℓ)Y)⁻¹. On a diagonal matrix with eigenvalues λᵢ, each determinant differentiation uses every row and column, yielding one factor ∏(1+|λᵢ|)⁻¹; this is ≤D^{−1/2}. Polynomial interpolation at integer Mellin parameters gives the general differentiated estimate. Integration by parts identifies all regularizations on the common far-right half-plane. Each one is holomorphic on its own larger half-plane. In unscaled two-by-two entry coordinates the differential operator has symbol (it)²(ab−c²−d²); a nonzero target of determinant zero illustrates the regularity condition.",
      "review": "Independently verified the scalar ((it)^n det B) and the domain 2 Re w+p+q+N>n² in the written proof. The determinant is required for division. The unregularized integral can converge on a larger half-plane for a particular test."
