    {
      "id": "AWH-03",
      "chapter": "lifts",
      "title": "Fourier inversion recovers the weighted coordinate Gram density",
      "anchor": "lifts-archimedean-density",
      "statement": "In the one-place Lebesgue normalization W(0)=(2π/|t|)^{n²}g(B), where g is the regular-locus Gram pushforward density. For M=2, n=1, signature (1,1), ℓ=1 and P=1 it is π exp(−2π|B|)/4. For nonzero B the continued value at w=−1 vanishes.",
      "hypotheses": "The coordinate density is required only on the open det B≠0. Insert N=n²+1 determinant derivatives at w=0. In the worked one-place example c=t=2π and both complex coordinates carry Lebesgue area.",
      "equations": [
        "lifts-archimedean-density-value"
      ],
